WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.501
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actress.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.534
You know her best from her work
in "Orange is the New Black."

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.701
She stars in "Dear Edward,"

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.834
which is available to stream
on Apple TV+.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.767
Please welcome back to the show
one of our favorites,

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.434
Taylor Schilling, everybody!

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.567
-Hello, Taylor!
-Hi, Seth!

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:33.667
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.367
-I'm so happy to be here
with you.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.834
-I want to ask a lot about
you and your projects,

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.901
but I do like to always start by
talking about your dog Tank.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.267
-Yes.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.801
-And you shared some photos,
and it does seem like Tank

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.534
is just holding up so well,
aging so well.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.567
Here's a photo of Tank up close.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.501
And if you're wondering what
Tank looks like farther away,

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:53.367
there's Tank
slightly farther away.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:57.667
How is Tank?
-He looks like Attila the Hun.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:00.267
-Yeah. Tank is --
Don't take this the wrong way.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:03.734
I found Tank to be a dog
with exactly one expression.

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.701
-She's working through it.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.000
You know what I mean?
This is what I love about Tank.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.834
Tank makes her way through.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.167
-Tank doesn't give up.
-Okay.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:15.400
Do you think that is because
you named her Tank?

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.767
-Yeah.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:17.968
-You put an
expectation upon her?

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.167
-She feel her own power.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.067
-And then,
when people are around her,

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.734
they can feel, in turn,
their own power.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.067
-Oh, interesting.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.133
She brings out the inner Tank
in other human beings?

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:28.734
-Yeah. That's how I feel.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.634
-Does she interact well
with other dogs?

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.200
-Um, no.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.634
-Okay.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.200
-No, but I'm always telling her,
"It's not your fault.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.868
It's mine."

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:40.534
And I tell other people that.
It's not her fault.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.100
It's mine. I didn't do it.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.767
-Oh, you didn't, like,
socialize her with other dogs?

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.801
-I didn't train her,
I don't think, properly.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.033
But, you know, she tries.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.200
-Okay.
-She tries.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.100
She does this move
where she like, "Pbht!"

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.367
And, like, puts her kind of butt
in the other dog's face.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.767
-Now, do you really -- Would you
describe that as trying?

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:00.801
I would call that sabotage,
I feel like.

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.968
-The other day,
a dog-sitter texted me and said

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:05.167
Tank started doing
her butt-in-the-face thing

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:09.801
but was jumping off of a bench
into a pile of larger dogs.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.167
So she said,
"We had to take Tank home."

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:15.968
-So Tank jumped and, in mid-air,
rotated herself so she --

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.367
That does not -- Tank does not
seem sort of the acrobatic type.

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.267
You said one of her dog-sitters.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.000
Does Tank kind of
go through them?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.434
-She needs help, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:28.667
-Yeah, she's special.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:29.968
-She's special?
-She's special.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:31.300
-Are you having a good --
I mean, is the new year

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.100
off to a good start
with you and Tank?

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.634
-I mean,
we've had some health scares.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:37.167
-Okay. You actually --
This is -- You have a photo.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:41.200
And I do want to say, this is a
dog mom with great concern.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.667
I mean this
with all genuineness.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.667
Like, it seems like Tank --
There you are.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.434
You seem - I should note,
you seem harried.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:52.934
Tank looks exactly the same.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.434
-This is a harrowing photograph.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.767
-So, what happened --
It's very nice.

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.701
I do appreciate that
something was wrong with Tank

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.100
and you did not stop for
hair and makeup on the way.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.133
Wait. What happened to Tank?
Why was --

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.200
-Well, I mean, now I'm
thinking it might be from

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.868
all of the, like,
sort of dive-bombing

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.300
into groups of other dogs.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.534
But she has -- You know,
she has a fragile back.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.367
-Yes.
-So, she needed -- Oh, God.

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:18.634
-Wait. So, what happened?

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.934
Now, obviously, something
happened that you thought,

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.501
"I'm going to wrap my dog
in a towel

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:23.968
and take her to a vet."

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.767
What was the moment
that you were like,

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:26.968
"Oh, no,
something is wrong with Tank"?

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.000
-[ Panting ]
-Okay.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.334
-Nonstop.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.934
-And that's more energy
than we usually get from --

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:32.634
-Yes, she was just
panting nonstop,

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:35.234
and I thought, "She needs help."

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.267
And she did.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.567
There was a problem
with her back.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.701
But she didn't need surgery.
She just needed drugs.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:40.934
-Okay.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:44.601
Taylor?

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:46.601
If I find out
you're using Tank...

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:50.767
If I find out
you're sending her out --

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:51.901
You're like,
"Throw your back out.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:54.100
Throw your back out, Baby Tank.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.434
Mom will take you to the vet.
50/50 split."

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.000
-Hell no, not today's take.
-Oh, yeah, that's true.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.601
Last time you were here,
you showed us

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:04.601
a photo of your apartment.

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:05.701
It was very scary.

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:06.934
The lights were
going on and off.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.334
-Yeah.
-Water was flooding.

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:10.334
-It seemed haunted.
-Yeah, it was.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.133
-And, you know, it's nice --
I actually thought it was nice,

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.667
because you think of
hauntings usually happening

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.067
out in the woods
and, like, cabins.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.601
It was nice that they
were moving into the cities.

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.367
Where are you now?

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.133
Do you feel better about
your current --

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:24.067
-I mean, it's an Airbnb still.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:25.133
It's better.
-Okay.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.734
-There's not --
Do you remember --

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:30.534
The shower came through the
ceiling in that other apartment.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:31.634
-Yeah.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:32.701
-That's not what
is happening here.

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.033
-Okay, that's good.
-It's nice.

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.501
Yeah, it's, like, settled.
We're settled, Tank and I.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:38.300
-I think one of the nice things
that you've done for yourself --

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.968
because, again, you've been here
multiple times --

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:44.334
is each subsequent apartment
is still terrible,

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:47.200
but it's so much better
than your last one.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.667
Like, you started at, like,
such a low floor.

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.000
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.567
-Yeah, like, I shared with you
a long time ago

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:56.334
about my first apartment.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:57.400
And now it's different.
Yeah, this one's different.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.501
-Your first apartment in
New York City,

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:00.100
where was the bathroom?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:03.434
-In the -- The bedroom and
the kitchen were the same thing.

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:05.701
-Okay.
-Yeah. The bitchen.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.567
-The bitchen, right.
-Yeah.

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:11.701
-So, you were sleeping in
a room with a stove.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:12.968
-Yeah.
-A working stove.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:14.734
-Yeah. And a sink and, like --

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.300
-Yeah. Like,
all the kitchen stuff.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.501
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.868
And, like, a dish rack.
-You've come a long way.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.167
-Yeah, yeah. Come on, like...

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:22.501
-You're doing alright
for yourself.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:23.634
-Thanks.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:25.000
-I want to talk to you about you

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.067
when we come back
after the break.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:27.300
That's more than enough
about Tank.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.400
I will be right back with
more from the wonderful

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.467
Taylor Schilling.

